<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stabiae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stabiae was an ancient town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a>, at modern Castellammare di Stabia. Destroyed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a> in 89 BCE during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a>, it became a resort of large seaside villas, which were buried by the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in 79 CE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a> died on its shore while trying to rescue people from the eruption. Villas such as the Villa San Marco and the Villa Arianna have been excavated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stabiae.jpg" alt="Stabiae" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wall_painting_from_Stabiae,_1st_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
